parts.stem:
A student carried out an experiment using Visking tubing to investigate osmosis. The student prepared a sucrose solution to represent phloem sap at the source. This was put into Visking tubing that was tied at one end, so that the tubing was approximately 75% full.

The rest of the procedure is summarised in Fig. 2.1. The tubing was removed after 20 minutes. The outside of the tubing was washed with distilled water, dried and weighed.

{{figure:figure-2-1-source-clean-v2.webp}}

